        "Walk tree at exact levels: level2 DATA DualDataList gets native entry, undefined ecuInfo and dual placeholder filename; level2 DATA HealthCheck gets web entry filename=level2 index+1; level3 records matching converter table get entry with level1 ECU info and index+1. Standard filename strips \\/:*?\"<>| from ECU name, then _FUNCTIONIDUPPERCASE+index+.csv. Dual uses base name or [BaseEcuName] and [DualEcuName]. Directory specificFolder+specificSubFolder+backslash+timestamp+_+trimmedVIN+backslash. Extension remains .csv even when content is TSV.",
        "When native entries exist, parameter.json path in output folder, mode0 write JSON. Payload includes connectionName GTS+CSV, URL reconstructed from first two // split elements, userProfile language and exact unit fields (speed/temperature/distance/weight/airflow/pressure types+values/vapor/fuel consumption), region, vehicle attributes, options, converted mileage, vin, productionDate formatted by dateFormatId1..6, productInfo, outputDataType, and paramList {srcFilePath:await mgr.getFullDataPath(storedId)+backslash+DATA,dstFilePath,functionId,storedDate:node+:00}. apendParamList uses await array.forEach(async...) rather than Promise.all; no stronger completion/order guarantee is claimed. Return {current:0,webCount,nativeCount,maxCount}.",
        "start launches native converter and sequential web conversion concurrently via Promise.all. Native is no-op if none, otherwise PF launchExternalApplication {execNo:6,execArg:parameterFilePath}. After both settle, if native count>0 wait2000ms then poll: getFolderInformation {path:outputFolder,includeFileList:[*.json]}; Object.keys(apiArgs).length===0 completes. Otherwise (or folder request failure) checkConnectionNameExist {name:GTS+CSV}; existNum>=1 continues, else completes; polling wait1000ms, no timeout. Check-connection failure rejects. Return {outputPath:specificFolder+subFolder+backslash+timestamp_VIN}; no native conversion content/success inferred from process disappearance.",
        "Web files sequentially getStoredData(storedId,true), initialize per-feature converter (Fuel gets resource), then viewDataToCsv(viewData,node,resource,outputDataType); HealthCheck instead writes one DTCHC per converted ECU with sanitized name and web.fileName index. Serialize rows to comma or tab joined cells, null/undefined=>empty and CRLF per row; no quoting/escaping, so delimiter/newline inside cell remains literal. writeFile mode1 prefixes BOM U+FEFF, explicitly catches failures and resolves. Per-file load/translation/convert failures are swallowed and do not stop later files; current++ only on successful converted write path (even swallowed write rejection counts). Always attempt version.csv from getStoredFileInfoData(true).gtsVersion or single space; errors swallowed.",
        "cancelProcess is public but not invoked by these stored controller CSV dialog flows: relayGuiMessage {name:connectionName,data:JSON.stringify({fromAppName:ScreenRelay.API_ID.GTS,commandId:99})}. It does not stop web loop or poll itself. healthCheckDataWriteProcess runs ECU writes sequentially and uses TSV/CSV serializer unchanged."
